    "coverLetter": "Dear Cano Team,\n\nI am writing to express interest in a future front-of-house opportunity with Cano. My hospitality experience includes Bar Lead and Server work, along with Private Event Coordinator and Private Event Server / Server roles at Capra’s. Those roles taught me to keep guest communication clear, support beverage service, and carry timing and event details reliably across a team.\n\nCano is particularly compelling because its current operation brings those lanes together. The official menu balances familiar Italian comfort with handmade gnudi con funghi and more composed seafood and steak choices, while the linked beverage menu gives the team real product knowledge to share with guests. I also recognize the restaurant’s public event route, where my coordination experience could be useful alongside daily floor service.\n\nI would bring calm organization, direct guest care and a willingness to learn Cano’s current food, wine and cocktail standards through the team’s own briefing process. I am interested in earning greater leadership responsibility over time through dependable front-of-house work and feedback, without overstating experience I have not held. I understand that a live role and application route must be confirmed before I apply.\n\nThank you for your consideration.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
