    "coverLetter": "Dear Osteria Giulia Hiring Team,\n\nI am writing to express my interest in a front-of-house opportunity with Osteria Giulia. My hospitality experience includes Server, Private Event Server, Private Event Coordinator, and Bar Lead work at Capra’s. Those roles taught me to combine attentive guest service with clear communication, product awareness, and calm coordination when a service or event changes in real time.\n\nOsteria Giulia stands out to me because its service has to carry real detail without losing warmth. The coastal focus of the menu—from Focaccia di Recco and trofie with pesto to seafood-led pastas—gives the team something specific to guide guests through, while the restaurant’s wine and cocktail recognition sets a high standard for beverage knowledge. I am especially interested in growing in an environment where menu fluency and thoughtful recommendations are part of the guest experience.\n\nMy Bar Lead work has made me comfortable taking responsibility for pace, communication, and guest-facing product conversations. My private-event coordination and service experience has also made me attentive to preparation, follow-through, and the details that make a planned experience feel seamless. I would bring that same discipline to a busy dinner service while continuing to learn the restaurant’s current Italian food, wine, and spirits programme.\n\nI am interested in building toward greater leadership responsibility over time, while earning that trust through dependable front-of-house work. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss whether my experience and approach could fit your team.\n\nThank you for your consideration,\nJonathan Beaulne",
