    "coverLetter": "Dear Actinolite Team,\n\nI am writing to ask whether you accept future front-of-house inquiries. I have worked as a Server, Bar Lead, Private Event Server and Private Event Coordinator, where I learned to keep guest communication clear, maintain dependable handoffs and stay calm as the pace of service changes.\n\nI am drawn to Actinolite’s daily-market approach and its belief that a generous meal can be an expression of neighbourly care. The balance between the $60 Neighbourhood Menu, the seasonal Full Menu and a simple wine-and-snack visit suggests a room where explaining a changing programme with warmth matters. I would learn the day’s food and beverage details carefully, communicate dietary information accurately and ask when I need to confirm something.\n\nMy private-event experience has also taught me to prepare thoughtfully, keep hosts informed and make handoffs clear when timing shifts. Over time, I hope to earn greater front-of-house responsibility through consistency, product knowledge and teamwork. I would welcome guidance on whether there is a suitable opportunity and the appropriate next step.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
