    "coverLetter": "Dear Alma Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for any appropriate future front-of-house, bar or event-service opportunity. My experience includes Bar Lead, Server, Private Event Server and Private Event Coordinator roles at Capra’s. It has taught me to read a table’s pace, communicate clearly when plans change, and make handoffs reliable for guests and teammates.\n\nI am drawn to Alma’s personal sharing style and to the care behind a menu that joins noodle and pasta traditions with a thoughtful wine list. I would learn the live menu carefully, use only confirmed product language, and ask rather than guess when a guest’s question needs kitchen or bar guidance. My event work has made me attentive to host priorities, detail and calm coordination.\n\nI understand Alma’s public talent invitation is not a posted role. If the team is considering future candidates, I would appreciate guidance on the appropriate next step. Over time, I hope to earn broader responsibility through dependable service, product learning and teamwork. I would bring a practical habit of preparing early, listening closely and following the team’s standards before trying to lead any part of service.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
