    "coverLetter": "Dear Le Baratin Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for a suitable front-of-house opportunity. My Capra’s experience includes Bar Lead and Server work, along with Private Event Coordinator and Private Event Server responsibilities. Those roles have made me attentive to clear guest communication, preparation and reliable handoffs when a service changes pace.\n\nLe Baratin interests me because its classic French cooking gives the floor something specific to explain: the sauce work, the table-d’hôte choices and a regional wine list. I would enjoy learning those details properly and helping guests choose comfortably, with enough information to feel looked after.\n\nYour two-seating dinner format also caught my attention. I understand how much early communication matters when a relaxed guest experience depends on several people keeping timing aligned. My event work has taught me to listen to the host’s priorities, keep colleagues informed and follow through when a plan changes.\n\nI would bring that same care to learning your operation. I am interested in earning greater responsibility through consistent service, product knowledge and feedback, including leadership or event duties where appropriate. If you are considering candidates now or for the future, I would welcome a conversation about the team’s needs and the best way to apply.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
