    "coverLetter": "Dear Giulietta Hiring Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for future front-of-house opportunities at Giulietta. My experience includes Capra’s Bar Lead and Server work, together with Private Event Server and Private Event Coordinator roles. In those positions I learned to keep guest communication clear, make reliable handoffs and remain composed when plans or pace change.\n\nI am drawn to Giulietta because its current programme calls for both polish and accuracy: a chef-bar setting in the heart of the action, seven wood-fired pizzas, pasta from cacio e pepe to corn scarpinocc, and a bar that moves from a $20 Marco Spritz to a focused Italian wine list. I would learn the live food, wine, cocktail and zero-proof details carefully, check before I guess, and help guests feel comfortable whether they are sharing pizza or building a longer meal.\n\nMy private-event responsibilities have also made me attentive to host priorities and clear communication when a plan changes. I would bring that same care to learning your service rhythm.\n\nI also hope to earn greater front-of-house responsibility over time through consistency, product knowledge and teamwork. If Giulietta is open to future consideration, I would appreciate the appropriate contact or application route.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
