    "coverLetter": "Dear Bar Isabel Hiring Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for a future front-of-house opportunity at Bar Isabel. My experience at Capra’s includes Bar Lead, Server, Private Event Server and Private Event Coordinator roles. That work has taught me to keep guest communication clear, make dependable handoffs, and stay composed when a room’s timing changes.\n\nI am drawn to Bar Isabel because its live programme asks for both energy and judgment. The menu moves from pintxos and Joselito ham to seafood, grilled octopus and larger plates, while the beverage list gives guests real choices: a dry Sherry flight, vermouth, cocktails, and Spanish whites such as Zárate Albariño and Valdesil Godello. I would learn the current list carefully, ask before I guess, and help guests build a shared meal that fits their appetite, pace and preferences.\n\nI also want to earn more leadership responsibility over time through product knowledge, reliable service and teamwork. My private-event background would help me communicate calmly with groups, while I understand Bar Isabel’s published model is intimate shared dining rather than private buyouts. If the team is open to future consideration, I would appreciate the appropriate contact or application route.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
