    "coverLetter": "Dear Quetzal Hiring Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for future front-of-house opportunities at Quetzal. My experience at Capra’s includes Bar Lead, Server, Private Event Server and Private Event Coordinator roles. I bring a service approach built on clear communication, dependable handoffs and staying calm as a room’s pace changes.\n\nQuetzal stands out because its current experience asks the floor to translate serious craft without losing warmth: in-house nixtamalized tortillas, wood-and-charcoal cooking, a curated menu, and a beverage programme that moves from agave cocktails to wines such as Viñátigo Listán Blanco from Tenerife and Langhe Nebbiolo. I would study the live menu carefully, verify details when unsure, and help guests find a meal and drink direction that fits their preferences and pace.\n\nMy Bar Lead background would support thoughtful beverage service, while my private-event work has made me attentive to planning, communication and group handoffs. I am also interested in earning greater leadership responsibility over time through product knowledge, reliability and teamwork. If the team is open to future consideration, I would appreciate the correct contact or process.\n\nI would welcome the chance to learn the team’s current standards and discuss whether my experience could support a future need.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
