    "coverLetter": "Dear Côte de Boeuf Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for future front-of-house opportunities. At Capra’s, my work has included Bar Lead and Server responsibilities, along with Private Event Coordinator and Private Event Server roles. Those experiences have taught me to balance warm guest service with careful pacing, clear team communication and attention to the details that matter when a dining room or event is moving quickly.\n\nCôte de Boeuf stood out to me because it brings together a bar à vin, butcher-shop craft, French bistro food and intimate private dining. I am especially interested in environments where the front-of-house team needs to learn changing product, describe it plainly and create a relaxed experience for guests arriving for anything from a glass at the bar to a longer dinner. I would be excited to build deeper wine and menu knowledge through that kind of service.\n\nMy private-event experience also feels relevant to the Butcher’s Table and shop dinners. I understand the importance of preparation, accurate handoffs and staying composed when timing shifts. I would bring that mindset to the floor while learning the team’s own standards and rhythm. Over time, I am interested in earning broader leadership responsibility through reliable day-to-day service and strong product knowledge.\n\nIf there is a suitable time to meet about future needs, I would appreciate the opportunity to introduce myself.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
