      "hospitality": "The official site confirms dinner, weekend brunch, a connected shop and two private spaces. The job description provides the sharpest detail of the service standard: one bartender runs a small high-end bar, serves bar-top guests through multiple courses, describes food and drinks, gives wine service and works with one support person. That is a hospitality system, not just a beverage station. The reasonable inference is that the team values calm sequencing, visible communication and accurate product handoffs. It is an inference from published duties, not a claim about every shift or every manager.",
      "ownership": "Ben Hodson and Roxanne Hodson are the best-supported founding ownership names. Ben’s Brix + Mortar Wine Co. background and current owner/wine-director references explain why wine is central, while current booking information gives Ben as the private-events contact. Henry’s Wine Shop describes itself as an independent shop connected to a single restaurant rather than a chain. The research does not prove every present-day corporate, equity or management arrangement; Jonathan should use “Henry’s team” unless he is introduced to a decision-maker.",
      "reputation": "A current OpenTable listing carries a restaurant response dated September 2, 2026 and recent guest comments praising service and wine, but crowd-sourced feedback is not proof of culture or service conditions. Star Wine List currently includes Henry’s as a Toronto wine bar and describes a Burgundy-focused, rotating-glass program. Those sources support that the room is visible in the current dining/wine ecosystem; they do not support a sweeping claim that it is universally acclaimed or an ideal employer. For a job conversation, actual role duties remain more useful evidence than review sentiment."
