    "coverLetter": "Dear Henry’s Hiring Team,\n\nI am applying for the part-time Bartender position at Henry’s. My work at Capra’s has included Bar Lead and Server responsibilities, as well as Private Event Coordinator and Private Event Server roles. Across those positions, I have learned to keep service organized while staying present with guests, communicate clearly with the floor team, and pay close attention to timing when several needs arrive at once.\n\nHenry’s appeals to me because the role is about more than producing a drink. The posting describes owning a small high-end bar, serving guests through a full meal, pacing multiple parties, speaking about food and wine, and working closely with support staff. That combination fits the kind of guest-facing responsibility I enjoy. I would bring a steady, detail-oriented approach to bar service and continue building product knowledge through the restaurant’s wine-focused environment.\n\nI am also drawn to the connection between the dining room, wine shop and private dining. My event experience has taught me the value of preparation, thoughtful handoffs and calm adjustments when timing changes. I would be glad to contribute that mindset wherever the team needs it. Over time, I am interested in earning greater leadership responsibility through reliable day-to-day service and deeper product knowledge.\n\nI would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background could support Henry’s bar and dining-room team.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
