    "coverLetter": "Dear Edulis Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for future front-of-house opportunities at Edulis. My experience includes Bar Lead and Server work at Capra’s, as well as Private Event Coordinator and Private Event Server/Server roles. I value the quiet work behind polished service: preparing carefully, communicating the right details, remaining attentive to guests, and knowing when to confirm something rather than guess.\n\nEdulis interests me because its menus follow the season and depend on seasonal ingredients and careful communication before guests arrive. That model requires a team that can learn the day’s courses, available supplements and confirmed guest information with precision. I would come ready to listen at pre-shift, take accurate notes and work respectfully with the kitchen and floor leaders. My bar and service experience has taught me how important clear handoffs are, and my private-event experience has reinforced the value of careful planning and calm adjustment.\n\nI am interested in earning greater responsibility over time through dependable service, product knowledge and coachability. I would welcome the chance to learn what Edulis looks for in a future FOH team member and whether my background could be useful.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
