    "coverLetter": "Dear Enigma Yorkville Hiring Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for a future front-of-house opportunity at Enigma. My experience at Capra's includes Bar Lead, Server, Private Event Server and Private Event Coordinator roles. That work has taught me to listen carefully, communicate clearly with guests and teammates, and follow through on details as a service changes.\n\nI am drawn to Enigma because the restaurant treats food, beverage and hospitality as one connected experience. I have been studying your seasonal tasting and à la carte formats, Saturday Interlude lunch, and the way your pairing philosophy is built into the menu from the beginning. I would learn the live food and beverage programme carefully, verify any detail I do not know, and help each guest feel comfortable with the pace and direction of their evening.\n\nYour private dining and buyout work also connects with my event background. I understand the importance of carrying guest preferences from planning into service, communicating changes early, and making dependable handoffs across the floor, bar and kitchen. Over time, I hope to earn broader leadership responsibility through product knowledge, consistent service and responsiveness to feedback.\n\nI would appreciate consideration for any future front-of-house role that matches my experience.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
