    "coverLetter": "Dear Buca Osteria & Bar Yorkville Team,\n\nI am applying for your Server opportunity. My experience at Capra’s includes Bar Lead and Server work, along with Private Event Coordinator and Private Event Server responsibilities. I value the preparation and communication that help a busy service feel welcoming: learning the product, listening carefully, keeping the team informed and following through when a guest needs something.\n\nBuca Yorkville interests me because the coastal-Italian menu asks servers to do more than take an order. Guiding someone from crudo to pasta, explaining the difference between raw tableside branzino and a grilled whole fish, and keeping seasonal ingredients accurate all require care. I would bring curiosity and disciplined preparation to learning your current menu, beverage list and service procedures.\n\nMy bar experience gives me a useful perspective on communication between the bar and dining room. My private-event work has also made me attentive to guest details, pacing and handoffs when a plan changes. I would welcome the chance to contribute those strengths to your floor team.\n\nI am interested in earning wider responsibility through dependable performance and continued learning. Thank you for considering my application; I would be glad to discuss the role and your expectations.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
