    "coverLetter": "Dear Joso's Team,\n\nI am writing to introduce myself for a future front-of-house opportunity at Joso's. My experience at Capra's includes Bar Lead, Server, Private Event Server and Private Event Coordinator roles. Through that work, I have learned to listen carefully to guests, communicate changes clearly and make reliable handoffs in a busy service.\n\nI am drawn to Joso's because its Dalmatian seafood service asks the floor to be both warm and exact. Your current menu moves from shared hand-stirred risotto and grilled octopus to whole fish chosen at the table. I would take the time to learn the current fish, preparation and beverage list from the team, check rather than guess, and help guests choose a meal that fits their appetite, comfort and pace.\n\nI also value the care required in a small restaurant: reservation details, clear expectations and composed service matter. My private-event background has made me attentive to those details, while my bar and server experience has taught me to keep guest communication simple and dependable. Over time, I hope to earn greater leadership responsibility through product knowledge, teamwork and consistent follow-through.\n\nIf there is an appropriate route for future front-of-house consideration, I would appreciate your guidance.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nSincerely,\nJonathan Beaulne",
